### Page 3 of 19

```text
Founded in 1978, Cheyenne Soccer Club is a volunteer soccer club with a
mission to promote youth soccer in Cheyenne, WY and Laramie County.
STING got its start in 1981, when it became apparent a competitive level of
soccer was sought by players and parents in the local recreational program.
Growth of a sport in a community doesn't just happen, but rather through
dedicated and passionate people who devote their time and effort into
developing a soccer club in Cheyenne, WY like the Cheyenne Soccer Club.
The club began TOPS (The Outreach Program for Soccer) in 2014. It is a
community-based training program for all athletes at any age with
intellectual, emotional, and or physical disabilities. The program strives to
provide soccer opportunities for players to develop at their own pace in a
safe, fun and supportive / inclusive environment.
CSC’s History
```

